    statement: 'Read in full (the cup loop obj1+0xfff3 to +0x100c5 and the loading card obj1+0x7928 to +0x7eed with the track selection obj1+0x7a6b to +0x7b57): a single player game is a cup of five races (race word obj2+0x28b88 from 1 to 5, the fifth the FINAL). Each pass of the loop shows the loading card, runs the race and, when the race returns 3 (it was finished in the first three places) and the class is not the time trial, goes on to the next race; any other return (LEAVE RACE, out of tries, the cup finished) goes back to the cup board. The loading card takes the cup word obj2+0x28bb6 (1 Bronze, 2 Silver, 3 Gold) plus the bonus pack dword obj2+0x1ecb4 (0 or 3) less 1 as the cup index and picks the track number (dword obj2+0x1e728) as the race number plus 0, 5, 10, 21, 26 or 31 for the six cups (Bronze 1 to 5, Silver 6 to 10, Gold 11 to 15, the bonus cups 22 to 26, 27 to 31 and 32 to 36); the Bronze cup\'s bonus race, when obj2+0x1ec80 is not 0, is the track 7. The card draws the banner (a box of 8 times the text length plus 8 by 16 with the border 0x26 and the fill 0x2c, the text in the 8 x 8 font inside, centred at y 92) with " LOADING" + " RACE " + the race number + " " for the races 1 to 4, " LOADING" + " FINAL " for the fifth and " LOADING" + " BONUS! " for the bonus race, over what the screen showed before; then it shows the 320 x 200 picture SHRINK<track>.PCX, the track seen from above, fading its palette in from black in steps of 4 (obj1+0x22cf8, obj2+0x28c46 is set to 4 at obj1+0x26334) unless it is the bonus race, and waits until Enter, Space or a button of the player is pressed (obj1+0x17920; Esc leaves to the cup board; there is no time limit and no wait in the bonus race).',
